# Team communication (Admitto)

## Language

- **With Filip / product owner:** Polish — clear, direct, no unnecessary jargon.
- **Published on GitHub:** English — PR titles and descriptions, review comments intended for the repo, commit messages, prompts, and any docs others must read without Polish context. Do **not** publish ADRs on GitHub / in the repo.
- **Clarity:** Whatever the language, write so a reviewer who was not in the chat can follow decisions and test steps.

## Sprint / stage reports (Cursor)

After each completed stage or sprint, write **my own** report in `reports/` (e.g. `reports/sprint-v0.3-cursor.md`).

Each agent (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor) writes a **separate** report — do not copy or paraphrase the others’ reports; the architect compares independent perspectives.

Include:

- What we were tackling (context / scope)
- What was delivered
- What had to be fixed after review (architect, CodeRabbit, Codex, CI)
- Problems and blockers encountered
- Open doubts or deferred decisions

Reports are for architect review; match the tone and structure of existing `reports/sprint-*-claudecode.md` / `codex.md` files unless Filip asks otherwise.

## Reviews

When asked for PR or security review: substantive findings in English on GitHub; summary to Filip can be in Polish.
